// # 28. What is an accessor property?

// An accessor property uses a getter and/or setter instead of a normal stored value descriptor.

// Example:

// ```js
// const user = {
//     firstName: "Bhavya",

//     get name() {
//         return this.firstName;
//     }
// };
// ```

// Accessing:

// ```js
// user.name
// ```

// executes the getter.

