// # 37. What is property shadowing?

// When an object's own property has the same name as an inherited property, the own property shadows the inherited one.

// ```js
// const parent = {
//     x: 10
// };

// const child = Object.create(parent);

// child.x = 20;
// ```

// Now:

// ```text
// child.x  → 20
// parent.x → 10
// ```

// The child's `x` shadows the parent's `x`.

// ---

// # 38. What happens after deleting the shadowing property?

// ```js
// delete child.x;
// ```

// The own property disappears.

// Then:

// ```js
// child.x
// ```

// again searches the prototype chain and finds:

// ```js
// parent.x
// ```

// So it returns:

// ```text
// 10
// ```

// ---

