// # 44. Is `Object.freeze()` deep?

// No.

// It is **shallow**.

// ```js
// const user = {
//     name: "Bhavya",
//     address: {
//         city: "Ahmedabad"
//     }
// };

// Object.freeze(user);

// user.name = "Rahul";
// user.address.city = "Mumbai";
// ```

// Typically:

// ```text
// user.name → "Bhavya"
// user.address.city → "Mumbai"
// ```

// The outer object is frozen, but the nested `address` object isn't automatically frozen.

