// # 45. Difference between `preventExtensions`, `seal`, and `freeze`

// ### `Object.preventExtensions()`

// Cannot add new properties.

// ### `Object.seal()`

// Cannot add or delete properties, while existing writable properties can still be changed.

// ### `Object.freeze()`

// Prevents adding/deleting and prevents changing existing data properties.

// And remember:

// > `freeze()` is shallow.

